WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:04.883
Ally stared at Mateo. "What kind of bad news?"

2
00:00:04.884 --> 00:00:11.269
"Let's sit down." Mateo led Ally to the dining room.

3
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:17.953
Ally sat. "Okay, I'm sitting, tell me the bad news."

4
00:00:17.954 --> 00:00:23.272
"Eclipses are not visible from everywhere on Earth," Mateo said.

5
00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:26.983
"We won't be able to see the next one here in Sandville."

6
00:00:26.984 --> 00:00:29.566
"That's okay." Ally shrugged.

7
00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:32.207
"I'll just go where I can see it."

8
00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:34.896
"Here's the thing," Mateo said.

9
00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:37.466
"You'd have to go to Patagonia.

10
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:40.192
It's very far away, in South America.

11
00:00:40.193 --> 00:00:42.786
You'd have to take a plane there."

12
00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:45.671
"I love flying," Ally said.

13
00:00:45.672 --> 00:00:50.126
"And it'll be fun to take an Earthlings' primitive jet."

14
00:00:50.127 --> 00:00:54.167
"Hmm. I guess that's possible," Mateo said.

15
00:00:54.168 --> 00:00:56.073
"Let's look at flights."

16
00:00:56.074 --> 00:01:01.576
While Mateo searched for plane tickets on his tablet, Ally sent Julius a text.

17
00:01:01.577 --> 00:01:04.034
Ally: Hi! Sorry about before.

18
00:01:04.035 --> 00:01:08.848
It looks like I might be taking a trip too!

19
00:01:08.849 --> 00:01:10.940
Julius: Cool! Where to?

20
00:01:10.941 --> 00:01:15.189
Ally: Patagonia. Have you ever heard of it?

21
00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.097
Julius: Sure. But why would you go there?

22
00:01:18.098 --> 00:01:21.570
Ally: Oh, no reason. I hear it's nice this time of . . .

23
00:01:21.571 --> 00:01:24.188
"Uh-oh," Mateo said.

24
00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:27.713
Ally looked up. "What now?"

25
00:01:27.714 --> 00:01:35.683
Mateo sighed. "A round-trip ticket from Sandville to Patagonia costs two thousand dollars."

26
00:01:35.684 --> 00:01:37.842
"That's all right," Ally said.

27
00:01:37.843 --> 00:01:42.021
"I have some money saved up from work, and your dad won't let me pay rent.

28
00:01:42.022 --> 00:01:48.571
So, between my savings and the money from the contest, I—" She gasped.

29
00:01:48.572 --> 00:01:50.999
"What's wrong?" Mateo asked.

30
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.408
"Silly me! I . . ." Ally could hardly get the words out.

31
00:01:55.409 --> 00:02:01.536
"I forgot that I spent all my money on the new phone and computer!"

32
00:02:01.537 --> 00:02:07.320
"Oh boy." Mateo shook his head, but then he perked up.

33
00:02:07.321 --> 00:02:11.788
"The computer was worth it though. Alpha is working now."

34
00:02:11.789 --> 00:02:17.533
"You're right. I wouldn't even know how to get my powers back without Alpha," Ally said.

35
00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:20.800
"I guess I'll just have to wait for the next eclipse.

36
00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:23.947
It has to be coming pretty soon, right?"

37
00:02:23.948 --> 00:02:28.515
"Let's see." Mateo tapped on his tablet.

38
00:02:28.516 --> 00:02:35.457
"I'm sorry, Ally. There won't be a solar eclipse visible here for eight years."

39
00:02:35.458 --> 00:02:42.363
"What?" Ally finished her text to Julius and got up to pace around the room.

40
00:02:42.364 --> 00:02:48.609
"I can't wait eight years! I have to find a way to get to Patagonia!"

41
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:50.723
Mateo looked up from his tablet. "I

42
00:02:50.724 --> 00:02:56.282
have more bad news. You need a passport to travel to another country." "A

43
00:02:56.283 --> 00:02:59.578
pass what?" Ally asked. "Passport.

44
00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:03.341
It's a document that comes from the government. It

45
00:03:03.342 --> 00:03:05.991
takes eight weeks to get one. There's

46
00:03:05.992 --> 00:03:08.517
lots of red tape." "Then

47
00:03:08.518 --> 00:03:12.018
they should take the tape off!" Ally snapped. "Besides,

48
00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:15.584
I can't go anywhere near the government. Dr.

49
00:03:15.585 --> 00:03:20.756
Lloyd is working with them, looking for aliens!" "Let's

50
00:03:20.757 --> 00:03:25.926
ask Alpha. I bet she can find a solution." Mateo

51
00:03:25.927 --> 00:03:31.309
covered his mouth as he yawned. Ally

52
00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.509
sighed. "You've had a long day, Mateo. Go

53
00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:42.231
to sleep. I'll get Alpha to work on it. She'll find the answer." Ally

54
00:03:42.232 --> 00:03:44.089
tried to sound hopeful. But

55
00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:47.193
inside all she felt was worry. "If

56
00:03:47.194 --> 00:03:55.397
Alpha can't help me, I'll have to get used to being a human!" she thought. ***

57
00:03:55.398 --> 00:04:01.088
The next morning at work, Ally was distracted.

58
00:04:01.089 --> 00:04:05.605
Alpha had promised to have an answer for Ally by the end of the day.

59
00:04:05.606 --> 00:04:11.767
"What if Alpha can't figure out how I can get to Patagonia?" she thought as she refilled saltshakers.

60
00:04:11.768 --> 00:04:15.423
"I can't stay on Earth for eight more years!"

61
00:04:15.424 --> 00:04:21.187
Soon Phil and Tina came in.

62
00:04:21.188 --> 00:04:26.014
"Two coffees and two of my regular breakfast sandwiches to go," Phil said.

63
00:04:26.015 --> 00:04:28.000
Tina looked very proud.

64
00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:33.023
"Phil's going to give me my own set of keys to the museum today."

65
00:04:33.024 --> 00:04:38.311
"Huh. That's nice for you." Ally sighed.

66
00:04:38.312 --> 00:04:41.192
"You okay, Ally?" Phil asked.

67
00:04:41.193 --> 00:04:43.882
"You're not your usual sunny self."

68
00:04:43.883 --> 00:04:48.921
"Of course, I'm myself," Ally said. "Who else would I be?"

69
00:04:48.922 --> 00:04:54.432
Tina laughed. "You're funny, Ally!

70
00:04:54.433 --> 00:05:00.020
Oh, I was wondering how that fancy new computer of yours is working."

71
00:05:00.021 --> 00:05:04.272
"Yes," Ally said. "Why do you keep—"

72
00:05:04.273 --> 00:05:07.999
"Ally! Your order is up!" Melanie called.

73
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.039
"Coming!"

74
00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:15.851
"Why does Tina keep asking me about the computer?" Ally thought as she picked up the order.

75
00:05:15.852 --> 00:05:20.690
"If I had my mind-reading powers, I could find out."

76
00:05:20.691 --> 00:05:24.525
Melanie watched Ally balance five dishes in her arms.

77
00:05:24.526 --> 00:05:27.328
"You sure you can handle all that at once?"

78
00:05:27.329 --> 00:05:32.847
"Of course I can!" Ally replied.

79
00:05:32.848 --> 00:05:37.034
But as she hurried to deliver the meals, she tripped over a customer's foot.

80
00:05:37.035 --> 00:05:40.840
"Great Galorpian goats!" Ally cried.

81
00:05:40.841 --> 00:05:49.892
The three plates of pancakes and two bowls of oatmeal flew up in the air before crashing down on the floor.

